    "title": "Billing service: choosing a database",
    "create_time": 1760000000.0,
    "mapping": {
      "root-c1a7e2f0-billing-db": {
        "id": "root-c1a7e2f0-billing-db",
        "message": null,
        "parent": null,
        "children": [
          "c1a7e2f0-billing-db-m0"
        ]
      },
      "c1a7e2f0-billing-db-m0": {
        "id": "c1a7e2f0-billing-db-m0",
        "message": {
          "id": "c1a7e2f0-billing-db-m0",
          "author": {
            "role": "user"
          },
          "create_time": 1760000000.0,
          "content": {
            "content_type": "text",
            "parts": [
              "We're building the billing service. Mongo or Postgres? We need invoices joined to customers and line items."
            ]
          }
        },
        "parent": "root-c1a7e2f0-billing-db",
        "children": [
          "c1a7e2f0-billing-db-m1"
        ]
      },
      "c1a7e2f0-billing-db-m1": {
        "id": "c1a7e2f0-billing-db-m1",
        "message": {
          "id": "c1a7e2f0-billing-db-m1",
          "author": {
            "role": "assistant"
          },
          "create_time": 1760000090.0,
          "content": {
            "content_type": "text",
            "parts": [
              "For relational data like invoices, customers and line items, Postgres fits better. You get joins, transactions and constraints. Mongo would push those joins into application code."
            ]
          }
        },
        "parent": "c1a7e2f0-billing-db-m0",
        "children": [
          "c1a7e2f0-billing-db-m2"
        ]
      },
      "c1a7e2f0-billing-db-m2": {
        "id": "c1a7e2f0-billing-db-m2",
        "message": {
          "id": "c1a7e2f0-billing-db-m2",
          "author": {
            "role": "user"
          },
          "create_time": 1760000180.0,
          "content": {
            "content_type": "text",
            "parts": [
              "Let's go with Postgres instead of MongoDB because we need joins and real transactions for payments."
            ]
          }
        },
        "parent": "c1a7e2f0-billing-db-m1",
        "children": [
          "c1a7e2f0-billing-db-m3"
        ]
      },
      "c1a7e2f0-billing-db-m3": {
        "id": "c1a7e2f0-billing-db-m3",
        "message": {
          "id": "c1a7e2f0-billing-db-m3",
          "author": {
            "role": "assistant"
          },
          "create_time": 1760000270.0,
          "content": {
            "content_type": "text",
            "parts": [
              "Good call. I'd also add the pgvector extension now if you plan semantic search later.\n\nNext step is writing the initial migration for customers, invoices and line_items."
            ]
          }
        },
        "parent": "c1a7e2f0-billing-db-m2",
        "children": [
          "c1a7e2f0-billing-db-m4"
        ]
      },
      "c1a7e2f0-billing-db-m4": {
        "id": "c1a7e2f0-billing-db-m4",
        "message": {
